INFO:MLEvolve:Reasoning: The predict path builds meta-features using p_cb as the average of CatBoost models 0-3 and p_cb_oh as model 4, but during training the OOF meta-features used a single default CatBoost model for p_cb and a single one-hot model for p_cb_oh, creating a train/inference mismatch that corrupts the stacked meta-learner. Additionally, the OOF stacking loop trains 4 models per fold (20 model fits) plus 8 final fits, which likely exceeds the 300s training budget. I'll align the inference meta-feature construction with training and reduce the model count to fit the time budget.
